The graph shows the height of a marked paddle on a waterwheel above the river surface over $12$ seconds, with the mean position drawn as a dashed line. What is the maximum height, and when does the paddle first reach its lowest point?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=10cm,height=6.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.5,xmax=13.4,ymin=0,ymax=3.4,xtick={0,1,...,12},ytick={0,0.4,...,3.2},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$ (seconds)},ylabel={Height (m)},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:12,samples=200] {0.8*cos(60*x)+2};
\addplot[dashed,domain=0:12,samples=2] {2};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
